findings.description:
The frontmatter has `dependencies: []`, but the slice cannot work without a released guide version that has a `copilot` case. The Risks section says an older guide "will fail at the script step with a clear error". However, the current `setupIdeAction` turns any non-zero exit into a generic "setup-ide exited with code N". How clear the error is depends entirely on what the old script prints. Under the failure-mode rule (every new I/O path needs an explicit, visible handling strategy), the design should:
- name the minimum guide version, or a way to detect support (for example, the script listing its supported targets);
- specify the user-facing message telling the user to run `cf guides update`;
- add a test for the "guide lacks copilot backend" path.
